        "max_width": 980,
        "heading": "<p>Your cells stopped hearing insulin</p>",
        "subheading": "<p>When you eat, insulin tells your cells to take the sugar out of your blood and use it for energy. <strong>Inositol is what carries that message inside the cell.</strong></p>",
        "caption": "Same knock. One of them gets answered.",
        "bottom_text": "<p>So your body knocks louder. More insulin, then more again. <strong>And high insulin does two things at once — it holds onto fat, and it pushes your ovaries to make more testosterone.</strong></p>",
